            The template is pre-built with formulas — you don't need to set anything up.
            It works as a complete <strong>student fee tracking Excel sheet</strong> with three sheets:
          </p>

          <h3>Sheet 1 — Monthly Fee Collection Format</h3>
          <p>
            The main sheet. Each row is one student. Columns run across the 12 months of the
            academic year (April to March). Enter the amount paid each month — the template
            calculates everything else automatically.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Student name, class, and monthly fee</li>
            <li>Payment columns for every month (Apr to Mar)</li>
            <li>Auto-calculated <strong>Total Paid</strong> per student</li>
            <li>Auto-calculated <strong>Total Due</strong> for the full year</li>
            <li>Status shows <strong>Paid</strong> or <strong>Pending</strong> automatically</li>
            <li>Summary bar: total students, total collected, total pending</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Sheet 2 — Attendance Register</h3>
          <p>
            Mark P (Present), A (Absent), or L (Leave) for each student per day.
            Works in uppercase or lowercase — colors update automatically.
            For a dedicated format, also see our
            <a href={attendanceLink}>free attendance register format for tuition classes</a>.
